---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site, url } from '../data/site';
const faqs = [
  [
    'Where can I download the application?',
    'Version 2.2.0 for Mac (Apple silicon, macOS 14.4 or later) is on the Download page, with its checksums and complete source. A new Windows version is being rebuilt and will follow.',
  ],
  [
    'Do I need an account or internet connection?',
    'No account is needed. Drawing processing takes place locally. The application does not use a cloud document service.',
  ],
  [
    'Does MARK change my original PDF?',
    'No. MARK adds temporary annotations over the page. Copying or exporting creates an image, presentation or new PDF. Save the review before closing if you want to keep it.',
  ],
  [
    'Do I need Microsoft PowerPoint?',
    'No. Creating a .pptx file happens locally. Open that file in a compatible presentation application. Some advanced Windows integration requires a running copy of PowerPoint and will be documented when Windows ships.',
  ],
  [
    'Why does Office to PDF ask for LibreOffice?',
    'This conversion delegates to a locally installed LibreOffice. Install LibreOffice from its official source. Other conversions and drawing viewing do not require it.',
  ],
  [
    'How does OCR work?',
    'On macOS, the current application uses Apple Vision for local text recognition. Windows OCR availability will be documented with the rebuilt release.',
  ],
  [
    'Can I use scanned PDFs and photographs?',
    'Yes. PDFs and PNG, JPEG, TIFF, BMP, GIF and WebP images are supported. HEIC/HEIF decoding is available on macOS. Scan with iPhone requires Apple Continuity Camera and compatible signed-in devices.',
  ],
  [
    'Which Mac or Windows versions are supported?',
    'The first Mac package targets Apple silicon. Its minimum macOS version is still being verified against the bundled libraries. Windows requirements will be confirmed with its rebuilt release.',
  ],
  [
    'How do I uninstall it?',
    'Remove the application. On Mac, local settings, cache and diagnostic logs remain under your user Library, in Application Support/ENG Drawing Viewer, Caches/ENG Drawing Viewer and Logs/ENG Drawing Viewer. Delete those folders if you also want to remove local preferences. Your drawings and saved scans remain where you saved them.',
  ],
  [
    'Can I report a bug with a confidential drawing?',
    'Please do not post private drawings to public GitHub Issues. Create a small fictional reproduction, remove identifying information, and review logs and screenshots before sharing.',
  ],
];
---

<Layout
  title="A little help, right here"
  description="Installation help, offline workflows, keyboard shortcuts and troubleshooting for ENG Drawing Viewer."
>
  <div class="container">
    <header class="page-hero">
      <div class="section-tag">SUPPORT</div>
      <h1>
        A little help.
        <br />
        <span>Right here.</span>
      </h1>
      <p>
        Answers for the everyday details, from your first drawing to your next
        presentation.
      </p>
    </header>
    <article class="page-content prose">
      <div class="faq">
        {faqs.map(([q, a]) => (
          <details>
            <summary>{q}</summary>
            <p>{a}</p>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
      <h2>MARK keyboard shortcuts</h2>
      <p>
        Tool shortcuts are the same on Mac and Windows. Use ⌘ on Mac and Ctrl on
        Windows for standard editing commands.
      </p>
      <table class="shortcut-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Tool</th>
            <th scope="col">Shortcut</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {[
            ['Select', 'V'],
            ['Pen', 'P'],
            ['Highlighter', 'H'],
            ['Text', 'T'],
            ['Arrow', 'A'],
            ['Outline circle', 'O'],
            ['Numbered callout', 'B'],
            ['Eraser', 'E'],
            ['Undo', '⌘ / Ctrl + Z'],
            ['Save marked PDF', '⌘ / Ctrl + S'],
          ].map(([n, k]) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{n}</td>
              <td>
                <kbd>{k}</kbd>
              </td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <h2>Still need a hand?</h2>
      <p>
        Include the app version, operating system, what you expected and the
        steps to reproduce the problem.
      </p>
      <a class="button" href={`${site.repo}/issues/new/choose`}>
        Report an issue ↗
      </a>
      <p style="margin-top:24px">
        <a href={url('download/')}>Release and installation information</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>
